 ### What It Does
 
-cli-opencode is the single routing point for runtimes that need an OpenCode dispatch. A smart router scores the prompt against intent signals (external dispatch, parallel detached, cross-AI handback, agent delegation, cross-repo) and loads only the references that match. On OpenCode 1 (1.19.3) the default dispatch is `opencode run --model opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash --variant max --format json --dir <repo-root>`. On OpenCode 2 (2.0.32) it is `cd <repo-root> && opencode2 run --standalone -m opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash#max --format json "<prompt>"`. A three-layer guard refuses self-invocation unless the request is an explicit parallel detached session.
